design\releases\0_0_2\B_027_github_manual_push_pending_loss.md:14:The B-002 fix gave GitHub mode true manual-push semantics: `commit()` creates real commits through the Git Data API and only `push()` moves the branch ref. But the pending chain head lives solely in the in-memory `pendingCommitHeads` map (`app/src/services/github_storage_service.ts`). Consequences:
design\releases\0_0_2\B_027_github_manual_push_pending_loss.md:16:- Reloading or closing the app in manual mode orphans every unpushed commit. The commits exist server-side as dangling objects, the app forgets their sha, and GitHub eventually garbage-collects them. Silent data loss.
