icy`.\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\test_support\\\\data_service_test_support.ts:119:        loadProjectConfig: vi.fn(async () => ({ backgroundShade: 'blue' as const, projectFolder: '', workingFolder: 'design' })),\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\test_support\\\\data_service_test_support.ts:122:        saveProjectConfig: vi.fn(),\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:14:Provide a custom dialog to easily edit the `affects` list of a card, with a dropdown of proposed repo files filtered on what is already typed.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:17:Still not implemented (confirmed by the 2026-07 implementation audit). `CardHeader.affects` exists as `string[]`, is parsed by `markdownParsingService` from `affects:` frontmatter lists and is searchable through F-017, and `markdownParsingService.rewriteListLines` already rewrites list fields generically (used for `agents:` references via `setAgentLogReferences`) — but there is no public affects-specific rewrite helper on `DataService`. The card UI (card view, body dialog, text view) has no `affects` editing surface. The storage contract (`StorageService` in `app/src/data/data_types.ts`) still has no repository file listing, so no suggestion source exists for either GitHub or local projects.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:23:- Add an affects editor dialog reachable from the card/editor UI. It shows current affected files, supports add/remove, and uses a typed file picker filtered by the current input.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_009_affects_editor.md:34:- Tests cover parsing-service header rewrite behavior, duplicate/self-path exclusion, filtered suggestions, and save flow from the dialog.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_019_telemetry.md:19:- Keep DSNs/app keys in untracked local config files or environment variables per subproject; tracked sample files may document required names but must not contain real keys.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_019_telemetry.md:29:- React and Electron initialize Sentry and Aptabase when local keys are configured, and run without telemetry failures when keys are missing.\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:4:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:48:const configuredProfileProvider: AgentCapabilitiesProvider = {\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:59:        const profile = findAgentProfile(configService.get('desktop.agentProfiles'), agent)\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.ts:79:    constructor(provider: AgentCapabilitiesProvider = configuredProfileProvider) {\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\github\\\\github_storage_types.ts:5:export const PROJECT_CONFIG_PATH = 'md2.config.json'\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:14:Provide a global theme service (light/dark, flat look, configurable color scheme with preview, configurable markdown styles with pre-built defaults) that all components refresh from, including reading the theme in Electron before the main window is created.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:17:Theming is minimal ([[F-004]]): `createAppTheme(mode)` in `theme/appTheme.ts` just returns `createTheme({ palette: { mode } })`, and `useThemeMode` (`theme/useThemeMode.ts`) tracks light/dark, persisting the choice to `localStorage` (`md2.themeMode`) with an OS-preference fallback. `App` builds the theme and provides it via MUI `ThemeProvider`; `mode`/`onToggleTheme` are threaded as props through `MainWindow` and `MainToolbar` rather than read from a service. There is no configurable color scheme, no flat/round/borderless styling, no markdown style config, and `CardTypeConfig` (`data/dataTypes.ts`) has no color. On the desktop, `desktop/main.js` creates the `BrowserWindow` with default chrome and never reads the theme, so the window buttons are unstyled.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:22:- Configurable color scheme: expose editable `primary`/`secondary`/… roles each with `light`/`regular`/`dark` variants, feed them into the palette, and offer a live preview while editing.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:23:- Configurable markdown styles: define a style config mapping each markdown section (title1, title2, caption, body, …) to font/color/size/formatting; ship pre-built defaults (`modern`, `classic`, `serif`, `sans-serif`, `handwritten`) selectable by the user.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:31:- The color scheme (primary/secondary/… with light/regular/dark variants) is user-configurable with a live preview, and the choice persists across restarts.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_018_styling_and_theming.md:32:- Markdown section styling is configurable, with the listed pre-built defaults selectable; the selection persists across restarts.\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:3:import { configService } from '../config/config_service'\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:33:        configService.clear()\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:61:    it('loads configured profile overrides and fixed thinking levels without provider credentials', async () => {\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:62:        configService.init({\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:63:            desktopConfig: {\\napp\\\\src\\\\services\\\\agents\\\\agent_capabilities_service.test.ts:100:        configService.init()\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_007_markdown_editor.md:17:`@mdxeditor/editor` is installed but still not used by any component in `app/src`; every editing surface is an interim multiline MUI `TextField`. Card view ([[F-005]]) and text view ([[F-006]]) are both implemented and wired through `ProjectWorkspace`, so `ProjectWorkspace` no longer edits a card directly — it delegates to `CardView` and `TextView` and forwards their changes to `DataService`. Card body editing goes through `CardBodyEditor` (used by the desktop `CardBodyDialog` and mobile accordion), whose `onBodyChange` calls `DataService.updateCardBody`; that method already uses the shared `markdownParsingService.replaceBody` to preserve the frontmatter/header block and replace only the body. Text view edits full file content in a per-tab `TextField` and saves via the same `onBodyChange`/`DataService` path. Both `CardBodyEditor` and the text-view editor carry TODO notes that the MDXEditor component and its formatting toolbar land with F-007 and replace them. There is still no shared editor component and no formatting toolbar (sticky or otherwise).\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_007_markdown_editor.md:23:- Replace the current `ProjectWorkspace` textarea path with the shared editor, then reuse the same component in card dialog/mobile accordion and future file tabs.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_017_search.md:21:The top shell is `MainToolbar` (MUI `AppBar`/`Toolbar`) rendered by `MainWindow`; it holds the \\\"MD²\\\" title, a config `IconButton` and a `toolbarAction` slot (currently `<ThemeControls />` from `app.tsx`). There is no search input in the toolbar. The desktop window is borderless via Electron `titleBarStyle: 'hidden'` with a `titleBarOverlay` in `desktop/main.js`; there is no manual CSS drag region (`-webkit-app-region`) anywhere in the React shell, so a custom drag bar and its non-draggable input/button zones do not yet exist.\\ndesign\\\\feature_descriptions\\\\F_017_search.md:23:Navigation into a card/file is local to `ProjectWorkspace`, which owns `viewMode` (`'cards' | 'text'`). `handleOpenInFileMode(path)` sets a `requestedPath` + `requestedNonce` and switches to text view; `TextView` opens